A||||4||Getaway2k||HELP!!!    INFO NEEDED FAST!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Getaway2k||04-05-2001||04:29 PM||||I take the Fiero out of storage today, fill up the tank at the pump (to the top of the neck-I know,..I shouldn't have done that), I look under the car and gas is leaking from what appears to be the top of the tank (steady trickle). It leaked steady for a good half hour, now it has stopped. The tank still reads on the full line. Is there a place on the top of the tank where the gas that I had in the neck would run out (as a result of over-filling the tank)? Do I need to have the tank checked form replacement/repair before driving?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||04-05-2001||04:46 PM||||There is an "O" ring on top of the tank where the cover plate for the fuel sender/pump is installed.  It may have dried up and shrunk a little while the car sat.  Since it has gotten moist with gasoline, it MAY have swelled up slightly and resealed itself.  The only way to access it is to drop the tank out of the car.  Keep a close eye on it--fuel falling out of the car is a baaaaadddd thing <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-05-2001||05:03 PM||||Unless you are storing the car for "years" you should leave the gas tank full. If not seals will dry out and cause problems. I fill mine up and toss in a shot of gasoline stablizer called "Sta-bil" Never had any problems.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||04-05-2001||06:51 PM||||  Keep a close eye on it--fuel falling out of the car is a baaaaadddd thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ya, and Fiero engine cmpt gets hot, and the fuel tank is rite in front of it !!!!!Could lite up like an afterburner !!!!!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-05-2001||07:00 PM||||The tank needs to be pulled and repaired ASAP. Fuel vapor is an even bigger danger than liquid. ||||reg||1
